      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! In the 5.5 to 7.0 pH range, grapevines find this soil pH ideal for the availability of essential micronutrients such as iron and manganese. At the lower end, slightly acidic soils (around 5.5) can lead to iron toxicity, but within this range, iron is typically mobile and accessible to plants. As for manganese, it becomes less soluble and hence less available at higher pH levels, but at the upper end of this range, manganese still remains available for grapevines. This balanced pH range optimizes the balance between micronutrient mobility and grapevine uptake, promoting healthy plant growth and grape quality.",
